@startuml component-architecture
!theme plain
title Walkthrough capture decomposition (ADR-0023)

package "Scope deciders (judgement)" {
  [qa-self\nwhich flows are evidence\nfor this PR] as QA
  [demo\nnarrative order,\naudience, polish] as DEMO
}

package "Foundation (mechanics)" {
  [recording + annotation] as REC
  [narration\ncues, clip keys,\nlicence disclosure] as NARR
  [stitching\nchapter cards,\noffset rebasing] as STITCH
  [clip contract\nffprobe'd real durations] as CONTRACT
}

database "Scenario library\n.feature — cases to draw from,\nnot a suite to execute" as LIB
database "narration cache\nkeyed (voice, lang, text)\noutside RUN_DIR" as CACHE

package "tt-e2e (standalone)" {
  [behave suite\nminimal annotation:\nscenario name + step bounds] as E2E
}

QA --> LIB : selects
DEMO --> LIB : selects
QA --> REC
DEMO --> REC

REC --> NARR
NARR --> CACHE : reuses across takes
REC --> STITCH : one clip per scenario
STITCH --> CONTRACT : rebases offsets from

E2E ..> CONTRACT : may emit\nthe same artifact shape

note right of E2E
  Runs in GitHub Actions with no agent
  present to repair a break, so it stays
  minimally annotated -- and it must NOT
  depend on the foundation skills.
  Consumption is one-directional.
end note

note bottom of REC
  One file PER SCENARIO, never one
  continuous take: the video finalises
  only at context.close(), so a late
  crash loses every earlier chapter's
  cue offsets.
end note

note bottom of QA
  Setup is proven before it is paid for:
  fixture probe -> synthesis -> filming.
  A caption is cued only after the state
  it claims is asserted.
end note
@enduml
